# Lien FX playbook

Research only. No orders. Full strategy tables: [docs/LIEN_FX_STRATEGIES.md](docs/LIEN_FX_STRATEGIES.md).

## Before any Lien technical setup

1. Call `classify_regime` (oanda-research) on the instrument. Default granularity **D**. Do not compute ADX, Bollinger, SMA, RSI, stochastics, or MACD in the model.
2. Match the play class to the result: `join_trend`, `fade_range`, or `breakout_watch`. If `trend_waning` is true, do not aggress.
3. Optional: `mt4_draw_regime` on a **matching** symbol/timeframe chart (prefix `sbox.regime.`). Oscillators stay in JSON; the overlay is bands, MA stack, 10-bar high/low, and a regime label. Paper/signal tickets: `mt4_draw_ticket` (prefix `sbox.ticket.`; hlines only, no orders).
4. Cite `lien-fx` via `rag-knowledge` (`search_knowledge` / `get_source_chunk`). Evidence is heuristic.

## Risk template (library, not MCP)

Prefer ≥ 1:2 R, ≤ ~2% equity (`app/risk.py`). Scale half at 1R, stop to breakeven, trail the rest. Never add to losers.

## Entry engines

Ch. 8 (Multiple Time Frames) is coded as the `entry_mtf` tool (oanda-research): higher-TF direction gate + lower-TF RSI-dip/rally trigger, run after the regime filter. Ch. 9 is `entry_dbb`. Ch. 13/14/16 are `entry_lien(chapter)`. Chapters 10, 11, 12, and 15 are not tools yet (news, session clock, `breakout_watch` paper policy); use the doc tables only after the regime filter.

